{"name":"Argyle","hex":"#348a5d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Argyle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of Argyll.","A surname."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of argyle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Argyle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Argyle, Victoria","blocks":[{"text":"Argyle is a locality in the City of Greater Bendigo in the Australian state of Victoria. At the 2021 census, Argyle had a population of 272. Argyle is named after a district pioneer."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argyle%2C_Victoria","wikidata":"Q109917941"},{"title":"Argyle County","blocks":[{"text":"Argyle County was one of the original Nineteen Counties in New South Wales and is now one of the 141 cadastral divisions of New South Wales. It includes the area around Goulburn. It is bounded by Lake George in the south-west, the Shoalhaven River in the east, and the Wollondilly River in the north-east."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Argyle_NSW.PNG/330px-Argyle_NSW.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argyle_County","wikidata":"Q4789817"},{"title":"Argyle (pattern)","blocks":[{"text":"An argyle pattern is made of diamonds or lozenges. The word is sometimes used to refer to an individual diamond in the design, but more commonly refers to the overall pattern. Most argyle contains layers of overlapping motifs, adding a sense of three-dimensionality, movement, and texture. Typically, there is an overlay of intercrossing diagonal lines on solid diamonds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/PinkArgyle.svg/330px-PinkArgyle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argyle_(pattern)","wikidata":"Q652490"},{"title":"Argyle (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Argyle is a surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Fiona Argyle, Australian politician","Jessie Argyle (1900–1955), Australian Aboriginal woman","John Argyle (1911–1962), British screenwriter, producer and film director","Michael Argyle (judge) (1915–1999), British judge","Michael Argyle (psychologist) (1925–2002), British social psychologist","Pearl Argyle (1910–1947), South African ballet dancer and actress","Stanley Argyle (1867–1940), Australian politician","Steve Argyle, American artist"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argyle_(surname)","wikidata":"Q37118538"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/County_of_Argyle_NSW_1840s.jpg/500px-County_of_Argyle_NSW_1840s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/County_of_Argyle_NSW_1840s.jpg/1280px-County_of_Argyle_NSW_1840s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/County_of_Argyle_NSW_1840s.jpg/500px-County_of_Argyle_NSW_1840s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1840s map of the County of Argyle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACounty_of_Argyle_NSW_1840s.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Sir_Henry_Raeburn_-_Colonel_Alastair_Ranaldson_Macdonell_of_Glengarry_%281771_-_1828%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Sir_Henry_Raeburn_-_Colonel_Alastair_Ranaldson_Macdonell_of_Glengarry_%281771_-_1828%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Sir_Henry_Raeburn_-_Colonel_Alastair_Ranaldson_Macdonell_of_Glengarry_%281771_-_1828%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Sir_Henry_Raeburn_-_Colonel_Alastair_Ranaldson_Macdonell_of_Glengarry_%281771_-_1828%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source